# =============================================================================
# Reader Studio Books - category rules
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is the place categories are defined. The catalog builder
# (`tools/build_catalog.mjs`) reads it on every run and turns each line into a
# "category rail" in the Reader Studio library.
#
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ADD A NEW CATEGORY
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Append one line, using the next free number:
#
#   CATEGORY_<n>=<slug>|<name>|<icon>|<match keys>|<description>
#
# Example:
#
#   CATEGORY_16=bangla-biography|বাংলা জীবনী|user-round|biography, bangla, memoir|বাংলা ভাষায় লেখা জীবনীগ্রন্থ।
#
# Fields (only SLUG and NAME are required):
#   <n>            Any unique number. Lines are applied in ascending order.
#   <slug>         Short ASCII id (a-z, 0-9, hyphen). It is written into the
#                  catalog and used in URLs, so pick it once and do not change
#                  it later.
#   <name>         Display name. Any language or script is fine.
#   <icon>         One of: rocket, search, ghost, wand, heart, compass,
#                  feather, scale, user-round, landmark, flask-conical, smile,
#                  book, book-open. Defaults to "book".
#   <match keys>   Comma-separated lowercase terms. A book is filed here when
#                  one of its subjects or tags contains a term. ORDER MATTERS:
#                  the FIRST matching category wins, so keep specific
#                  categories above broad ones (keep "liberation-war" above
#                  "history").
#   <description>  One line shown on the category rail.
#
# Notes:
#   - A line whose first non-space character is `#` is a comment. Blank lines
#     are ignored. Fields are separated by `|`; a single field may contain
#     commas.
#   - A book can also be pinned to a category from its sidecar, which always
#     wins over the match keys:
#         books/<name>.meta.json  ->  { "category": "<slug>" }
#   - Point the builder at a different file with the CATALOG_CATEGORIES
#     environment variable.
# =============================================================================

CATEGORY_1=science-fiction|Science Fiction|rocket|science fiction, sci-fi, sci fi, space travel, dystopia, time travel, space opera|Futures, inventions and the consequences of discovery.
CATEGORY_2=mystery|Mystery|search|mystery, detective, crime, murder, sherlock|Detection, deduction and the puzzle of crime.
CATEGORY_3=gothic|Gothic|ghost|gothic, horror, ghost, vampire|Dread, the uncanny and the shadow of the past.
CATEGORY_4=fantasy|Fantasy|wand|fantasy, magic, myth, legend|Magic, myth and imagined worlds.
CATEGORY_5=romance|Romance|heart|romance, love stories|Love, longing and the ties between people.
CATEGORY_6=adventure|Adventure|compass|adventure, voyages, seafaring|Voyages, quests and the open world.
CATEGORY_7=poetry|Poetry|feather|poetry, poems, verse, sonnet|Verse and lyric.
CATEGORY_8=philosophy|Philosophy|scale|philosophy, ethics, logic, metaphysics|Arguments about meaning, mind and conduct.
CATEGORY_9=biography|Biography|user-round|biography, autobiography, memoir, diaries, letters|Lives told whole.
CATEGORY_10=liberation-war|মুক্তিযুদ্ধ ১৯৭১|landmark|liberation war, muktijuddho, bangladesh, 1971|বাংলাদেশের মুক্তিযুদ্ধ নিয়ে লেখা বই।
CATEGORY_11=history|History|landmark|history, historical, war, civilisation, civilization|The documented past.
CATEGORY_12=science|Science|flask-conical|science, physics, biology, chemistry, mathematics, astronomy|Nature, experiment and explanation.
CATEGORY_13=children|Children|smile|children, juvenile, fairy tale, nursery|Stories written for young readers.
CATEGORY_14=religion|Religion|book|religion, bible, christian, islam, quran, spiritual|Faith, scripture and reflection.
CATEGORY_15=fiction|Fiction|book-open|fiction, novel, literature, classic|Novels and stories.
